@description Rea-Pods
@author Frank Acklin
@version 0.1.1
@changelog
  - Windows x64. Tested with Windows 11, REAPER 7.66 and AirPods.
  - macOS: no changes.
@provides
  [darwin] reaper_rea-pods.dylib https://github.com/acklin83/reaper-scripts/releases/download/rea-pods-v$version/$path
  [win64] reaper_rea-pods.dll https://github.com/acklin83/reaper-scripts/releases/download/rea-pods-v$version/$path
@about
  # Rea-Pods

  REAPER extension for macOS and Windows. Plays REAPER's output on AirPods, or on any other output device, while REAPER keeps running on its audio interface. Both play at the same time.

  ## What it does

  - Takes REAPER's hardware outputs 1/2 (selectable), the same signal that goes to the audio interface
  - Corrects the clock drift between the two devices itself, so no aggregate device is needed
  - Starts playing as soon as the AirPods connect, and waits when they are gone
  - Uses only the AirPods' output. If another app opens their microphone, the system switches them to headset quality until that app lets go
  - Settings panel, floating or docked: on/off, device, source outputs, volume, buffer

  ## Actions

  - Rea-Pods: Mirror output to AirPods (on/off)
  - Rea-Pods: Show settings panel (dockable)
  - Rea-Pods: AirPods volume +1 dB / -1 dB
  - Rea-Pods: Show status

  ## Notes

  - Bluetooth adds a delay on the AirPods: fine for listening, too late for recording.
  - The settings panel needs **ReaImGui** 0.10 or newer (via ReaPack). The mirror itself runs without it.

  ## Requirements

  - macOS 12 or later, universal binary (Apple Silicon and Intel). Tested with REAPER 7.86.
  - Windows x64. Tested with Windows 11 and REAPER 7.66.
